Kotlin/Native

Parts of kmicro are derived from the Kotlin/Native runtime of the Kotlin compiler, version 2.4.21
(https://github.com/JetBrains/kotlin, tag v2.4.21, kotlin-native/runtime/src), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. Its source files carry JetBrains copyright lines ("Copyright 2010-2024 JetBrains s.r.o. and Kotlin
Programming Language contributors." in the current file header, "Copyright 2010-2018 JetBrains s.r.o." and similar in
older files), and the NOTICE file of the Kotlin compiler (license/NOTICE.txt in that repository, licenses/NOTICE.txt
in the Kotlin/Native distribution) reads:

   =========================================================================
   ==  NOTICE file corresponding to the section 4 d of                    ==
   ==  the Apache License, Version 2.0,                                   ==
   ==  in this case for the Kotlin Compiler distribution.                 ==
   =========================================================================

   Kotlin Compiler
   Copyright 2010-2024 JetBrains s.r.o and respective authors and developers

The kmicro files derived from it, with the upstream files they follow (under kotlin-native/runtime/src/):

    runtime/dtoa/            main/cpp/dtoa/: copied; dblparse.cpp, fltparse.cpp and cbigint.h are modified, and
                             runtime/dtoa/README.md lists the changes
    runtime/kmicro.h         declarations and data layouts of main/cpp/Runtime.h, Memory.h, TypeInfo.h and the
                             other files its first comment names
    runtime/init.c           main/cpp/Runtime.cpp, main/cpp/Memory.h: runtime start, initializer list, TLS records
    runtime/init_cxx.cpp     main/cpp/Runtime.cpp: CallInitGlobalPossiblyLock, CallInitThreadLocal
    runtime/mm.c             mm/cpp/RootSet.cpp, mm/cpp/ShadowStack.cpp, gc/common/cpp/MarkAndSweepUtils.hpp,
                             main/cpp/Runtime.cpp (globals)
    runtime/numbers.c        main/cpp/Operator.cpp
    runtime/kmath.c          main/cpp/KotlinMath.cpp
    runtime/strings.c        main/cpp/KString.h, KString.cpp, ToString.cpp, Console.cpp
    runtime/types.c          main/cpp/Types.cpp, Natives.cpp, Boxing.cpp, Arrays.cpp
    runtime/interop.c        main/cpp/Natives.cpp: Kotlin_interop_malloc, Kotlin_interop_free

Apart from runtime/dtoa, these files are written for kmicro in C or C++: they implement the same runtime interface,
with the same data layouts and behaviour, and their comments name the upstream sources they follow. Any other
kmicro file whose comments name a Kotlin/Native source it follows is derived in the same way.

